## Lore

Leopard Men are the most feared warriors among the Haven Mutants: quick to
anger, merciless to anyone they count as an enemy, and willing to pen captured
outsiders as food or sell them to Horune Pirates and Splugorth Slavers. Now and
then even another mutant ends up in those pens.

The Guardia tribe is the extreme of the race. Its warriors treat the White Rose
knights and the people of the Garden''s as thieves who took the Garden from the
mutants, ignore clan borders when they hunt or raid, and will take outsiders
that another clan is sheltering. Pressure from the other clans keeps them mostly
at home, though raiding bands of 1D4+2 still slip out. The other Leopard Men
clans share the attitude with less defiance, and most of them cooperate with the
other mutants to keep the peace.

Violence is their first answer to any problem, and the other mutants think of
them as barbarians. Yet they are clever planners and cunning tacticians, and
among their own people they can be gentle, thoughtful and loving. Their hatred
of outsiders grew out of generations of persecution and of watching visitors go
mad. They accept the Shamans'' teaching that mutants are humanity''s chosen next
step, blame humans and their machines for the Great Cataclysm, and keep
advanced technology and magic at arm''s length.

A Leopard Man is short and heavily muscled, with a human build, spotted skin,
dark fur at the backs of the lower legs and a great mane around the jaw, chin
and back. The head is a cat''s: pale blue eyes and an enormous toothed mouth.

## Mutant Shaman

Any sizable clan is led by a Shaman, and a Leopard Man may be one. The
**Leopard Man Shaman** variant carries the Shaman''s attribute and P.P.E. gains
and adds the Shaman skills. What the app does not do for it:

- The Shaman skills **replace all Secondary Skills, all Piloting skills and all
  modern W.P.s**. A Shaman never uses a modern weapon, vehicle or machine. Drop
  those picks by hand.
- **Commune with the Mighty Lady.** The Shamans now worship Isis and may pray to
  her. A *prayer of strength* is heard on 01-20%, +5% per level: it gives +6 to
  P.S., +1D4x10 M.D.C. and 48 hours without food or water, and may be tried six
  times a year. A *prayer of inspiration or wisdom* is heard on 01-12%, +3% per
  level (+10% after a week of fasting) and answers with a dream vision of
  insight, an idea or a warning.
- **The Shaman levels on its own ladder**, the Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman
  table on printed 79: 0, 2,351, 4,701, 9,401, 18,801, 28,001, 38,001, 53,001,
  77,001, 102,001, 143,001, 195,201, 240,401, 310,601, 360,801.

Shamans are also the lawmakers, judges and leaders of their clans.

## GM Notes

Most Leopard Men prefer bone weapons and traditional melee arms, but will carry
an energy rifle and love Vibro-Blades and Neural-Maces. They use outsiders''
vehicles and machines only when they must.

They keep to their own clans more than most mutants and wish the others would
fight invaders harder. They are stockpiling weapons and supplies for the war
with the outside world they believe is coming. Of the other mutants they like
the Savage Lummox and the Mantis Men best. They trade often with Horune
Pirates, Slavers, Barbarians and, quietly, the Shemarrians, giving arms, vehicles
and captives in return for tools, unusual weapons and mounts, liquor, news,
gold and gems, and trust none of them. They count as enemies any outsider or invader, ghosts and the Undead Horrors, monsters, magical creatures and madmen. They live on the
surface in wooded areas, high ruins and the walls of cavernous ruins.

Size is 5 feet to 5 feet 10 inches (1.5-1.75 m) and weighs 170-200 lbs (76.5-90 kg). They could reach 100, but warrior life cuts most males short at 1D6+36
and females at 2D6+44. Average NPC level is 1D6+4; a player character starts at
level one or two.

**A secret.** The Guardia Leopard Men and the Eastside Mantis Men have been
quietly founding camps beyond Madhaven, unknown to the other mutants: 98
Leopard Men and 78 Mantis Men near Jersey Side, 20 of each in Maryland, and a
dozen Leopard Men with half a dozen Mantis Men among the Montreal pirates. They
are militant anti-human survivalists who hunt, raid and slave-trade, and they
have contacts with the Shemarrians, pirates and some D-Bee bands in the East.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'leopard-men');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'leopard-men';

